Renderer: the blend-splits bits of a pipeline are set only for directional lights that have a shadow

The field they are read from is written only for such a light; for the others it held whatever the memory did,
so the same scene asked for different specialized pipelines from one run to the next. The shader reads the bit
only for a light that has a shadow. Against godotengine/godot 4.7.2-stable (ed1daf0).

diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/light_storage.h b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/light_storage.h
index 71043e4..5998327 100644
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/light_storage.h
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/light_storage.h
@@ -837,7 +837,9 @@ public:
 	uint32_t get_directional_light_blend_splits(uint32_t p_directional_light_count) const {
 		uint32_t blend_splits = 0;
 		for (uint32_t i = 0; i < p_directional_light_count; i++) {
-			if (directional_lights[i].blend_splits) {
+			// Written only for a light that has a shadow, and read by the shader only then: left out otherwise, the
+			// bit is whatever the memory held, and pipelines differ from one run to the next for no visible reason.
+			if (directional_lights[i].shadow_opacity > 0.001 && directional_lights[i].blend_splits) {
 				blend_splits |= 1U << i;
 			}
 		}
